{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1021450-vampires-dreaming","id":1021450,"title":"Vampires Dreaming","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-23T18:31:49-08:00","id":1021450,"title":"Vampires Dreaming","content":"Do vampires dream in VtR 2nd ed? It states somewhere in passing that they don't in the same way. What does that mean?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4135-blue-thomas","name":"Blue Thomas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4135_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T04:58:16-08:00","id":1021943,"title":"","content":"I think there was some obscure passage in 1E material hinting that a dreaming vampire's consciousness drifts into the Underworld. Cool and thematic, but no idea how it'd work out in 2E, especially since we haven't seen the Underworld in-depth without Geist 2E. Or was this about vampires in torpor?<br /> <br /> Either way, if they don't dream the same way as humans do, then maybe their consciousnesses lie stiff like a corpse and are impenetrable to dream-invading powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T05:43:59-08:00","id":1021953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blue Thomas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1021450-vampires-dreaming#post1021450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do vampires dream in VtR 2nd ed? It states somewhere in passing that they don't in the same way. What does that mean?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If it's anything like 1E, it's probably because the Beast is always in the dream somewhere. That always twists the dream somehow as it's always injecting its own instinctual hopes and fears.<br /> <br /> I also read from DaveB somewhere that vampires aren't alone in this-all supernatural beings, barring mages, dream, but they lack a(n inherent) way to get to the Temenos, the universal unconsciousness, or an accessible Oneiros, the pocket of the dream that exists whether they sleep or wake. That latter trait is more of a boon, as people can really fuck you over in your Oneiros.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T06:04:44-08:00","id":1021956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1021450-vampires-dreaming?p=1021953#post1021953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I also read from DaveB somewhere that vampires aren't alone in this-all supernatural beings, barring mages, dream, but they lack a(n inherent) way to get to the Temenos, the universal unconsciousness, or an accessible Oneiros, the pocket of the dream that exists whether they sleep or wake. That latter trait is more of a boon, as people can really fuck you over in your Oneiros.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weeeellllll, technically, the Temenos and the Oneiros have nothing to do with whether one can dream or not. They're poetically referred to as &quot;the realm of dreams&quot;, with &quot;oneiros&quot; literally meaning 'dream', but they're not actually about dreams. They're about souls. Human souls, specifically. You can look at a dream being dreamed inside someone's Oneiros while that someone is sleeping, and probably manipulate a dream from insdie the Oneiros, but that's about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T23:38:43-08:00","id":1026360,"title":"","content":"The merit 'Dream Visions' suggests that vampires do dream by some means, though it could be a specific strangeness with the mekhet blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11516-forgelineage","name":"ForgeLineage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11516_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T02:23:28-08:00","id":1026415,"title":"","content":"Looking under the torpor section of 2e it mentioned that torpor dreams were strange and nonsensical, and these dreams kept the vampiric mind active and exercised. It also mentioned that these dreams prepare the vampire for waking up in a new world, and that it sometimes went awry with the vampire waking up a whole new person or with distorted memories. While I know it's torpor, but I can't imagine the daysleep being much different except for the length of time.<br /> <br /> Now, my personal take on it is that the dreams are strange and nonsensical is because it's when the Beast is out to play; seeing as most Kindred try to actively prevent frenzy (can't be eating their neighbors in the throes of it) I've come to imagine that the Beast gets to essentially play when the vampire is asleep. This also comes with the added cost (some would say benefit) that when some entity tries to enter their dreams expecting to deal with the vampire as he typically is they will instead be dealing with the vampire's Beast and all it entails.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T07:20:56-08:00","id":1026495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1021450-vampires-dreaming?p=1026415#post1026415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking under the torpor section of 2e it mentioned that torpor dreams were strange and nonsensical, and these dreams kept the vampiric mind active and exercised. It also mentioned that these dreams prepare the vampire for waking up in a new world, and that it sometimes went awry with the vampire waking up a whole new person or with distorted memories. While I know it's torpor, but I can't imagine the daysleep being much different except for the length of time.<br /> <br /> Now, my personal take on it is that the dreams are strange and nonsensical is because it's when the Beast is out to play; seeing as most Kindred try to actively prevent frenzy (can't be eating their neighbors in the throes of it) I've come to imagine that the Beast gets to essentially play when the vampire is asleep. This also comes with the added cost (some would say benefit) that when some entity tries to enter their dreams expecting to deal with the vampire as he typically is they will instead be dealing with the vampire's Beast and all it entails.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Torpor is not your average nightly &quot;sleep&quot; though. Torpor is like a near death experience. And the dreams you experience in torpor are referenced as &quot;torpor dreams&quot; several times. To me, that seems to imply that it is not a normal thing. Like fever dreams are not your average dreams and do not happen every time you sleep. <br /> <br /> Waking up is like death in reverse. It is painful, your body doesn't work right, your limbs are numb ect. I would think on the average normal night if you &quot;die&quot; for the night, then the average normal vampire would not dream. I figured the Dream Visions merit made the Mehket special in the sense that they dream or there are a few devotions that force dreams upon the victims.<br /> I don't allow things to enter a vampire's dreams unless they have caused those dreams to happen.<br /> <br /> I think that Torpor Dreams are nonsensical because say if you slept for 100 years, there is no way your brain ( or your player ) would remember all the information and sensory details that went by. All the things that changed, all the sounds you heard would be fleeting blurbs. Like listening to a song on fast forward, it makes no sense, but you might pick out a word or two here and there. <br /> <br /> Then again, I do not interpret the beast to be a separate entity that can go off and do things or make rational choices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T13:34:43-08:00","id":1026669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1021450-vampires-dreaming?p=1026495#post1026495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then again, I do not interpret the beast to be a separate entity that can go off and do things or make rational choices.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't interpret the Beast as a separate entity, but I admit that looking at my words makes it seem so. I interpret the Beast as a vampire's pure Instinct, and in their daysleep the Man, or how a vampire normally acts, is not at the helm. So kindred dreams are basically when their instincts are acting out, and that's where the part of the Beast getting to play comes in. Instincts are never rational, and that isn't the Beast's job; the Beast is a vampire's instincts that keep them existing from night to night.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T10:04:35-08:00","id":1027728,"title":"","content":"I think you can force a vampire to dream with the Wet Dreams devotion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}